  <data name="bt_ValidatePdf.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scans all PDFs in the Output Ready folder and matches
each one to a student record using name + fuzzy matching.

✅  Matched PDFs  → ready for upload
⚠️  Unmatched PDFs → copied to 6_Error for manual review

Produces Validation_Results.csv — review it before
generating the Upload CSV.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="bt_GenerateCsv.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reads Validation_Results.csv (produced by Validate PDFs)
and generates Upload_to_PHIS.csv for Phase 3.

✅  Validated records  → added to Upload CSV
⚠️  Missing PDFs       → skipped and logged
📋  FileRose records   → appended automatically

Run 'Validate PDFs' first, review errors,
then click this button to prepare the upload.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="bt_Upload.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Final step — uploads all validated consent forms
and FileRose documents directly to PHIS client records.

Prerequisites:
  ✅  Phase 1 complete  (Client IDs resolved)
  ✅  Phase 2 complete  (PDFs validated)
  ✅  Upload_to_PHIS.csv generated

Chrome will open and log into PHIS automatically.
Uploads in batches — progress is saved after each record.

⚠️  Do not close the browser window during upload.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="bt_AppendFileRose.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scans the FileRose output folder for renamed PDFs
and appends missing rows to Upload_to_PHIS.csv.

✅  Safe to run multiple times — duplicates are never
    written twice (checked by ClientID + DocumentTitle).

Use this when FileRose PDFs were not ready during
Generate Upload CSV, or to add them later.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="txt_OriginalDigitalConsentCount.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter the total number of digital consent submissions shown for this school/grade batch on the SNB website. This value is confirmed manually by the uploader/verifier. Phase 4 does not access the SNB website.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="txt_ExpectedFileRoseCount.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter the number of physical FileRose forms identified in the original school batch. Each scanned FileRose PDF page represents one physical FileRose form; multiple pages in one PDF are separate forms merged before upload.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="btn_VerifyDocumentsOnPhis.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Confirms that eligible Verification_Upload.csv document titles are currently present on PHIS. This read-only verification does not upload, archive, or modify CSV files.</value>
  </data>
